      "description": "Watch Rosario Central vs Racing Club highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 29, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina showcased a match of high stakes and intense physical duels as Rosario Central took on Racing Club . Both sides aimed to gain a foothold in a contest where tactical discipline and defensive resilience were paramount from the opening whistle. A Crucial Breakthrough Before the Break On July 29, 2026, the match began with a cautious approach from both sides, as they looked to avoid early errors. The first half was characterized by heavy challenges in the midfield, leading to the first booking of the night for Santiago Sosa in the 39th minute. The deadlock seemed destined to hold until the teams reached the locker rooms. However, in the first minute of stoppage time (45+1'), Racing Club found the breakthrough they had been searching for. A clinical finish put the visitors ahead just seconds before the halftime whistle, drastically altering the momentum of the game and putting the pressure squarely on the hosts for the second period. Tactical Shifts and Substitution Flurry As the second half commenced, Rosario Central looked to respond by introducing Facundo Mallo . The managers soon turned to their benches to inject fresh energy into the game. Racing Club brought on the likes of Tomás Conechny and Matías Zaracho , while the hosts introduced Franco Cervi and Federico Navarro to bolster their creative options. Despite the tactical changes, clear-cut chances remained at a premium as the game grew increasingly physical. Late Drama and a Flurry of Cards The final twenty minutes saw the referee take center stage as the intensity boiled over. A string of yellow cards followed, with Ignacio Rodríguez , Nazareno Colombo , and Giovanni Cantizano all being cautioned. As the clock ticked down into added time, the desperation of the closing stages led to further bookings for Marcos Rojo , Ezequiel Cannavo , and Baltasar Rodríguez , highlighting the fierce nature of this closely contested battle."
